# Contributions of Socialization Theory to Consumer Behavior Research

**Authors:** Ward, Scott

## Abstract
Socialization theory can contribute to consumer research because it focuses on (1) youth and development, (2) interaction of factors affecting consumer behavior, and (3) linkages between mental processes and overt behavior. Various approaches to socialization research and consumer research are described, including cognitive development and learning-theory approaches. (Author/AV)

